-- title:
--   Divisibility of Pic⁰ of the reduced level-N modular function field
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $q$ a prime with $q \nmid N$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$, in the sense that the image of $q$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ belongs to the nonunits of $A$, and write $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ for its residue field. Inside the Laurent series field $k((\mathsf q))$ consider the intermediate field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$ over $k$, generated by the two elements $\mathrm{jqModC}\,k = \mathsf q^{-1}\cdot(\text{image in } k[[\mathsf q]] \text{ of the integral power series } \mathrm{jNum})$ and its image $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k\,N$ under the substitution $\mathsf q \mapsto \mathsf q^{N}$; thus the field $k(j(\mathsf q), j(\mathsf q^{N}))$. Its group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ is, by definition, the quotient of the group of divisors of degree zero — finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued functions on the places of this field over $k$ whose total degree vanishes — by the subgroup of principal divisors. The assertion is that for every nonzero natural number $n$ and every class $c$ in this $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ there is a class $c'$ with $n \cdot c' = c$; that is, the degree-zero divisor class group is divisible.
--
--   This is the divisibility of the Jacobian of the level-$N$ modular curve in characteristic $q$ for $q \nmid N$, obtained by reduction from the divisibility of $J_0(N)(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$. It is used in the construction of torsion preimages under the component map attached to a place specialisation of a model of the modular curve.
